{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27264908","formula":"C₃₀H₃₂ClF₃N₂O₂","hill":"C30H32ClF3N2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O","F","Cl"],"composition":{"C":30.0,"F":3.0,"H":32.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Fluperamide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Fluperamide is a synthetic opioid structurally related to loperamide, developed as a potent antidiarrheal agent. Like loperamide, it acts primarily as a peripherally selective μ-opioid receptor agonist, effectively reducing gastrointestinal motility and fluid secretion without significant central nervous system effects due to limited blood-brain barrier penetration. Fluperamide’s pharmacological profile was designed to maximize antidiarrheal efficacy while minimizing the risk of opioid-related side effects and abuse potential, a strategy that has contributed to the development of related compounds in the phenylpiperidine class."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":131534,"mass":545.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C)C(=O)C(CCN1CCC(CC1)(C2=CC(=C(C=C2)Cl)C(F)(F)F)O)(C3=CC=CC=C3)C4=CC=CC=C4","inchikey":"WPYGCZCMGMVGNO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-[4-[4-chloro-3-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-4-hydroxypiperidin-1-yl]-N,N-dimethyl-2,2-diphenylbutanamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"131534","atoms":70,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":8.419,"y":-1.836,"z":-1.289,"el":"Cl"},{"x":7.367,"y":1.201,"z":1.779,"el":"F"},{"x":8.332,"y":-0.732,"z":1.588,"el":"F"},{"x":8.775,"y":0.847,"z":0.16,"el":"F"},{"x":3.059,"y":1.927,"z":-0.671,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.13,"y":0.694,"z":2.206,"el":"O"},{"x":0.07,"y":0.166,"z":0.336,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.59,"y":-0.9,"z":2.764,"el":"N"},{"x":2.919,"y":0.52,"z":-0.428,"el":"C"},{"x":2.45,"y":0.294,"z":1.028,"el":"C"},{"x":1.832,"y":-0.019,"z":-1.385,"el":"C"},{"x":1.014,"y":0.769,"z":1.282,"el":"C"},{"x":0.428,"y":0.495,"z":